# === Ready-Run (Three.js web build) ===
# esbuild's bundle-analysis metafile — regenerated by `npm run build`.
build-meta.json
# Playwright diagnostic screenshots — regenerated by `npm test` / `npm run release`.
# These are evidence for a single run, not source; committing them just churns the diff.
tests/shots/
# msys/Git-Bash crash dumps
*.stackdump

# === CCGS process scaffolding (not part of the game) ===
# 2.3 MB of Unity/Godot-oriented agents, skills, hooks and slash commands. This project is
# Three.js, so none of it applies to the code here — see CLAUDE.md, which supersedes it.
# Machine-local anyway: the hooks shell out to paths that only exist on one workstation.
.claude/
CLAUDE.ccgs-reference.md
# 62 files of Unity/Godot API reference shipped by the same framework. Keeping it would
# actively mislead a contributor into thinking this is a Unity project.
docs/engine-reference/
# Per-directory CCGS standards files. They route work to Unity/Godot specialists and point
# at docs/engine-reference/, which is excluded above — shipping them would leave a
# contributor following instructions to a directory that is not in the repo.
docs/CLAUDE.md
design/CLAUDE.md
src/CLAUDE.md
docs/COLLABORATIVE-DESIGN-PRINCIPLE.md
docs/architecture/tr-registry.yaml
# Remaining CCGS framework documentation: worked examples about crafting systems and
# combat damage, plus registries driven by its slash commands. Generic framework material,
# not documentation of this game.
docs/examples/
docs/WORKFLOW-GUIDE.md
docs/registry/
production/
src/.gitkeep
